Notification of Award. It is expected that a decision selecting the successful
proposer will be made within one (1) week of the closing date for the receipt for proposals. Upon
conclusion of final negotiations with the successful proposer, all proposers submitting proposals
in response to this REP will be informed in writing of the name of the successful Proposer.
III. SCOPE OF SERVICES
A. Provide legal advice and consultation relating to tax and other legal matters associated
with the financing for the Municipal Court as set forth in the ballot initiative, as well
as advisability of combining the financing of the Municipal Court with other ballot
initiative-approved projects.
B. Provide a legal opinion(s) with respect to the authorization for and issuance of any debt
obligations, questions relating to tax matters and adherence to legal requirements under
federal andlor state laws and regulations. Such opinion shall include but is not limited
to an opinion as to the validity of and tax-exempt status of any bonds issued to finance
the project.
C. Draft and review legal documentation including all required resolutions, financing
documents, closing documents and transcripts and coordinate the authorization and
execution of those documents.
D. Provide ongoing legal services in matters relating to interpretation of applicable
regulations, applicable statutes or pending litigation arising out of municipal finance
counsel services provided in response to this REP.
3
