It is recommended that the proposal be organized in the format listed below.
A. Briefly describe the firm’s history and principal areas of practice.
B. Describe the firm’s practice in the following areas:
a.
Public finance, particularly with regards to Wyoming governmental financing;
b.
Governmental bonds or borrowing;
c,
Compliance with applicable federal securities laws and regulations;
d.
Practice areas other than public finance.
C. Describe the knowledge and experience of the attorneys who would be assigned to the
City’s transaction(s), particularly the individual(s) who will be the City’s primary
contact(s), and include the resumes of these attorneys.
D. Describe comparable financings during the past five years in which the firm has
served as municipal finance counsel or in a similar role. Provide contact information
for five clients represented by the firm in similar roles for reference purposes.
E. If you have noted unique, complex, or challenging issues in connection with the
proposed financing, indicate how the experience and expertise of your firm will be
utilized to complete the necessary legal work.
F. Compensation:
a.
Describe your firm’s proposed compensation. All fees will be contingent upon
the completion of appropriate financing.
b.
Based on the amount of financing anticipated from the ballot initiative at issue,
provide a non-binding estimate of the total approximate fees for service in this
matter.
