Re:
Municipal Finance Counsel Services
Ladies and Gentlemen;
The purpose of this engagement letter is to set forth certain matters concerning the role we
will serve and the responsibilities we will assume as municipal finance counsel to the City of
Cheyenne, Wyoming (the “City”) in connection with the proposed issuance ofbonds or obligations
(the “bonds”) as described in the City’s Request for Proposals number RFP-l-18 distributed
October 2, 2017 (the “RFP”).
SCOPE OF ENGAGEMENT
In this engagement, we expect to perform duties relating to the issuance of one series of
bonds, as well as to provide ancillary advice following the issuance of such bonds.
In particular, and in accordance with the City’s RFP and our response thereto dated
October 19, 2017 (the “RFP Response”), we would expect to provide the following legal services,
in accordance with our professional responsibilities as municipal finance counsel and industry
standards, with respect to any such bonds:
1.
Provide the City with legal advice and assistance on (a) financing structures
and techniques, options and methods, including payment terms, credit enhancement and
bond specifications; (b) federal and state tax matters as they relate to the City’s financing;
and (c) federal and state securities issues as they relate to the City’s financing. Ifrequested
by the City, we can also assist in its process relative to selecting an underwriter andlor
fmancial advisor.
4828-2268-9873.4
